    <h1>STABILITY KEGS NITRO COFFEE</h1>
    <p class="muted">By John Goerke. <time datetime="2017-12-01">December 1, 2017</time> (updated <time datetime="2018-11-16">November 16, 2018</time>). Category: News Nitro Coffee and Nitro Tea.</p>

    <p>This is a historical article, kept as originally framed in 2017. The commercial positioning below describes Bona Fide's offer at that time under the historical pricing model.</p>

    <h2>The Bona Fide Elegant Solution</h2>
    <p>The Bona Fide Elegant Solution positions shelf-stable kegs as a way to reduce the usual barriers to serving nitro coffee: shelf stability, costly equipment, maintenance and keg deposits.</p>

    <h2>Good to the last drop, with predictable COGS</h2>
    <p>The product is presented as good to the last drop, with predictable cost of goods sold. Each keg delivers a known quantity of nitro brew, and the article refers to a better-than-industry-standard gross profit under the historical pricing model.</p>

    <h2>Tap and pour</h2>
    <p>Service is tap and pour, with minimal training and no coffee preparation on site.</p>

    <p>Read more about <a href="/nitro-coffee-kegs/">nitro coffee kegs</a> and <a href="/how-ambient-stable-coffee-kegs-help-you-save-more-money/">ambient stable coffee kegs</a>, or return to the <a href="/blog/">blog</a>.</p>
